{
  "name": "Turn new blog posts into AI-written social drafts checked against each network's rules",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Turn new blog posts into social drafts that every network accepts\n\nFor content marketers who want a social post for every new article without checking each network's rules by hand.\n\n### How it works\n1. Every hour the workflow reads your RSS feed and keeps only articles it has not seen before.\n2. Claude writes a short caption for each one.\n3. Preflight checks the caption and the link against the rules of every channel you chose: length counted the way each network counts it, link and hashtag rules, plan limits.\n4. If a network would refuse it, Claude rewrites it once using Preflight's exact reasons (for example \"Text is 385 characters; Bluesky allows 300.\") and Preflight checks again.\n5. Captions that pass are saved in Preflight as **drafts** for a person to approve. Nothing is published.\n\n### Setup\n1. Needs the verified community node **Preflight** ([n8n-nodes-preflight](https://www.npmjs.com/package/n8n-nodes-preflight) 0.1.1 or later): search for Preflight in the nodes panel and choose Install. Tested on n8n 2.43.\n2. In [Preflight](https://preflight.social) (the free plan works), connect your social accounts, then create an API key under Settings → API keys with the scopes `posts:read` and `posts:write`. That key can make drafts but can never publish. Add it as a **Preflight API** credential in the three Preflight nodes.\n3. Add an Anthropic credential to **Claude**.\n4. In **Configuration**, set your feed URL and your channels, e.g. `bluesky, mastodon, linkedin`.\n\n### Customization\n- Change the caption rules in **Write caption** (tone, hashtags, language).\n- Swap Claude for any chat model.\n- Send **Still refused** to Slack or e-mail so someone writes those by hand.",
        "height": 880,
        "width": 560,
        "color": 1
      },
      "id": "c88af001-075a-515c-8f12-94a87bd7ab89",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -760,
        -380
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 1. New articles\nReads the feed and skips anything seen in an earlier run. At most three per run, so a long backlog does not flood your drafts.",
        "height": 360,
        "width": 1100,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "cbd85a4c-b30f-518f-868f-f6de2f15bb5e",
      "name": "Section: new articles",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -60,
        -160
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 2. Caption and rules check\nClaude writes the caption; Preflight answers `ok` or a list of issues per network.",
        "height": 520,
        "width": 680,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "6ef64f58-bca3-5953-9bd5-d3f8912d15d6",
      "name": "Section: caption and check",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1080,
        -160
